I’ve isolated the two concrete lifecycle defects. I’m changing the adapter so session-wide libssh2 state machines use a bounded cancellation-aware gate, and bridge teardown closes the injected connection, cancels and joins every service task, then discards buffers—eliminating the late-completion race instead of merely hiding its counter.
