The server log showed a real adapter defect: the custom transport callbacks returned `-1` plus `errno`, but libssh2’s callback ABI expects the negative socket error value itself (the pinned C harness correctly returns `-EAGAIN`). That made ordinary would-block look like a disconnect. I’m correcting the callback contract and its regression assertions.
